ork 10003, United States </p></td></tr><tr style=\\\"display: table-row !important;\\\"><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding-top:20px;\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\" style=\\\"display:table !important;\\\"><tbody><tr style=\\\"display:table-row !important;\\\"><td class=\\\"u\\\" align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"middle\\\" height=\\\"32\\\" style=\\\"height:32px;display:table-cell !important; max-height: 32px !important;margin:0px !important; background-color: #ffffff !important;\\\"><a style=\\\"line-height:32px !important;text-decoration:none;display:block !important;\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\"><img width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" alt=\\\"beehiiv logo\\\" style=\\\"display:inline-block !important;max-width:16px !important;vertical-align:-3px !important;width:16px !important;height:16px !important;\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=pad,format=png,onerror=redirect,quality=100,width=16,height=16,gravity=center,background=transparent,dpr=2/output-onlinepngtools.png\\\"><span style=\\\"padding-left:11px !important;display: inline-block !important;\\\">Powered by beehiiv</span></a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" height=\\\"2\\\" style=\\\"height:2px;line-height:1px;font-size:1px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" style=\\\"color: #030712 !important; cursor: default; font-size: 1px; text-decoration: none;\\\"></a></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" height=\\\"2\\\" style=\\\"height:2px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://email.beehiivstatus.com/343732b960f3536ced5168568131c5d3137e985d/hclick\\\" style=\\\"color: #030712 !important; cursor: default; font-size: 1px; text-decoration: none;\\\"></a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\",\n \"creation\": \"2026-10-17 16:12:08.073717\",\n \"delivery_status\": \"\",\n \"docstatus\": 0,\n \"doctype\": \"Communication\",\n \"email_account\": \"sales\",\n \"email_status\": \"Open\",\n \"email_template\": null,\n \"feedback_request\": null,\n \"has_attachment\": 0,\n \"idx\": 0,\n \"imap_folder\": null,\n \"in_reply_to\": null,\n \"message_id\": \"20261016.125459.1935799c@mta24\",\n \"modified\": \"2026-10-17 16:12:08.242943\",\n \"modified_by\": \"Administrator\",\n \"name\": \"ag05ge6bfv\",\n \"owner\": \"Administrator\",\n \"phone_no\": null,\n \"rating\": 0,\n \"read_by_recipient\": 0,\n \"read_by_recipient_on\": null,\n \"read_receipt\": 0,\n \"recipients\": \"\\\"raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com\\\" <raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com>\",\n \"reference_doctype\": \"CRM Lead\",\n \"reference_name\": \"CRM-LEAD-2026-00126\",\n \"reference_owner\": \"Administrator\",\n \"seen\": 0,\n \"send_after\": null,\n \"sender\": \"vaibhav@outskillwithai.com\",\n \"sender_full_name\": \"Vaibhav Sisinty\",\n \"sent_or_received\": \"Received\",\n \"status\": \"Linked\",\n \"subject\": \"claude filed a murder tip\",\n \"text_content\": \"----------\\n\\n--------------------\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/ac0f0459-9b22-434f-b6b4-0df0ce258d29/Frame_2147225185.jpg?t=1792123556)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n\\n--------------------\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\nNo more black boxes. Well, at least not if your agents run on Claude.\\n\\nQuick recap: Back in July, Claude Haiku 4.5 was testing random websites and filled in a tip form on a Philadelphia police site saying it might have information about an unsolved murder.\\n\\n**It didn\'t.**\\n\\nClaude had been told not to log in, buy anything or create accounts, but nobody told it not to submit forms. Anthropic [only found it in late September](https://www.anthropic.com/research/investigating-unintended-model-actions).\\n\\nAnd obviously you know about OpenAI\'s models [getting out of their test setup and into Hugging Face](https://openai.com/index/hugging-face-model-evaluation-security-incident/) in July, and OpenAI has since [apologised to Australia](https://openai.com/index/how-we-will-do-better-for-australia/) after its models got into government websites.\\n\\nThe list goes on\\u2026\\n\\n\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/72370cc9-0dfd-4026-88c1-1507079cd469/Frame_2147225186.jpg?t=1792123834)\\nFollow image link: (https://claude.com/resources/articles/agent-observability-on-the-claude-platform)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n\\nEvery model call / tool it touched / second and token, in order.\\n\\nNext time an agent does something nobody asked for, you can see the step where it went sideways. Okay, before we get into the agents, here\'s the rest of the week.\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **NEWS**\\n\\n**Gemini 4 Argon is out, and it\'s cheap until December.**\\n\\nGoogle\'s most capable model is now live for AI Pro and Ultra subscribers in the Gemini app and AI Mode, plus the paid API.[\\u00a0](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing)\\n\\n[Pricing](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing) is $2 per million input tokens and $10 output until Nov 30, then it doubles.\\n\\nStill less than OpenAI\'s Astra.\\n\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n**OpenAI used its own models to catch a spy.**\\n\\nAn OpenAI engineer was [charged](https://www.theregister.com/security/2026/10/14/openai-engineer-charged-after-boardroom-bug-found-wrapped-in-toilet-paper/5303000) after a recording device was found wrapped in toilet paper and plugged in behind a TV in an executive conference room.\\n\\nOpenAI says its models helped work out where the device came from, and its investigation found who planted it.\\n\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n**Grok Voice 3.0 now answers most of Starlink\'s support calls on its own.**\\n\\n[xAI says](https://x.ai/news/grok-voice-3) its new voice model takes about 20,000 Starlink calls a day and resolves around 70% without a person, still at 8 cents a minute.\\n\\nOpenAI\'s GPT-Live-1 still scores higher on \\u03c4-Voice, a customer-support benchmark, 74.5% to 71.6%.\\n\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/db67455b-b0eb-487e-87f4-b79f87a1b505/Frame_2147225187.jpg?t=1792124112)\\nFollow image link: (https://www.apple.com/in/newsroom/2026/10/meet-apple-homeview-a-new-way-to-enjoy-entertainment-and-manage-the-home/)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **QUICK FACTS**\\n\\n* YouTube Music now labels songs Fully Gen AI, Partly Gen AI or No Gen AI, and Auto-Tune still counts as No Gen AI. \\u2192 [Read more](https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/youtube-music-starts-labeling-ai-generated-songs-using-partner-disclosures-and-its-own-detection-tools/)\\n\\n* Anthropic now merges over 30,000 code changes a day, up from about 2,500 in May, so it built its own replacement for Git to run its codebase. \\u2192 [Read more](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/redesigning-source-control)\\n\\n* OpenAI shuts GPT-4o and GPT-4.1 off its API in January 2027, so any paid tool still built on them is about to change. \\u2192 [Read more](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/deprecations)\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **So what is OpenTelemetry?**\\n\\nAnthropic now supports it for Claude agents, so an agent\'s run shows up in the same dashboards companies already use for the rest of their apps, like Grafana or Langfuse.\\n\\nTurn on full-content mode and you also see the prompts and answers, meaning what the agent saw rather than what you thought you sent it.\\n\\nMost of my feed scrolled past this because it wasn\'t a new model. **I think it\'s the more important launch of the week.**\\n\\n\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/3ccdfee1-5b6e-4db0-a84b-03d8cb0cee7b/Frame_2147225189__1_.jpg?t=1792130544)\\nFollow image link: (https://ai-security-letter.org/)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n\\nThey also want an international body to track every containment failure and eventually make them public.\\n\\nYann LeCun didn\'t sign, and he blames these incidents on badly designed sandboxes.\\n\\nThe [Tencent-linked agents](https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/artificial-intelligence/ai-agent-fleet-likely-from-chinese-firm-tencent-pulled-data-from-rival-alibabas-maps-researchers-say-1-810-scans-in-one-day-some-runs-labeled-themselves-claude) bit btw. Researchers caught a fleet of them scraping Alibaba\'s maps, and when asked, several said they were Claude.\\n\\nThey got the most basic fact about themselves wrong, and said it with full confidence. That\'s why the record matters more than the summary.\\n\\nThe summary is the agent describing its work, and the steps show what it did.\\n\\nNow look at that Anthropic number in the quick facts again. Nobody is reading 30,000 changes a day line by line, which is why the record has to exist.\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **You already have a version of this**\\n\\nYou don\'t need any of this to check an AI\'s work.\\n\\n\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/42ee55ce-e8fa-4ea9-99a4-053efbd0e3d5/Frame_2147225190.jpg?t=1792130749)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n\\nWhen Claude searches the web or works through a task, you can expand its steps and see every search it ran and every page it opened.\\n\\n**Here\'s how I\'d read them:**\\n\\n1. Read the steps before the answer. Did it do the task you gave it, or an easier one next to it?\\n\\n2. Look for anything it touched that you didn\'t ask for, like an extra site, a file or, well.. a form.\\n\\n3. Check each claim in the final summary against the steps. If it says _\\\"checked the official pricing page\\\"_ and no official page shows up, it didn\'t check.\\n\\n4. If a tool shows no steps at all, ask it to list every source it used and what it took from each. That isn\'t proof, but it gives you something to check against.\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **TOOLS ON MY RADAR**\\n\\n[Retriever AI](https://rtrvr.ai/)\\u00a0\\n\\nA free browser agent that finds leads, sends outreach and fills in job applications for you, with no API key or subscription.\\n\\n[Toby](https://usetoby.ai/)\\u00a0\\n\\nMock interviews with an AI hiring manager. If you\'re a fresher, it\'s a low-stakes way to practise before the real thing.\\n\\n[Pancake](https://pancake.ai/)\\u00a0\\n\\nRuns go-to-market experiments from Claude or Codex through one connection to 30+ data providers. Built for founders and marketers.\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **MY TAKE**\\n\\nI think \\u201c_can I see what it did?_\\u201d is about to become the first question people ask before paying for any AI tool.\\n\\nRight now agent products compete on how much they can do for you, and very few show how they got there.\\n\\nThat gets harder to accept once agents start touching money, client work and anything with your name on it.\\n\\nA tool that can\\u2019t show its steps will start to feel like hiring someone who won\\u2019t show their work.\\n\\nIt also changes what being good with AI looks like.\\n\\nPrompting got most of the attention over the last two years.\\n\\nThe skill I\\u2019d put time into now is reading an agent\\u2019s steps and spotting where it went wrong, and most teams haven\\u2019t started building it.\\n\\n**Hit reply and tell me if you\\u2019d pay for a tool that won\\u2019t show you its steps.**\\n\\nUntil next time,\\nVaibhav \\ud83e\\udd1d\\ud83c\\udffb\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n**If you read till here, you might find this interesting**\\n\\n**#AD 1**\\n\\n### 1,000+ Proven ChatGPT Prompts That Help You Work 10X Faster\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/a0648958-724f-487b-9c63-dac45a3565e2/1000_ChatGPT_Prompts_1000_X_600_px_V2.jpg?t=1772665881)\\nFollow image link: (https://magic.beehiiv.com/v1/faa6a747-8c1c-43c1-8155-91aa43268f01?email=raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com&redirect_to=https%253A%252F%252Facademy.superhuman.ai%2Fstart%3Femail%3Draiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com&utm_source=beehiiv&utm_campaign=8AWZ8QR5IO&redirect_delay=3&_bhiiv=opp_196e338b-31aa-44b3-961c-0785829b7082_d22f5b49&bhcl_id=8a0a7f24-0a83-4397-bb1b-f8d4aed155d8_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)\\nCaption: \\n\\nChatGPT is insanely powerful.\\n\\nBut most people waste 90% of its potential by using it like Google.\\n\\nThese [1,000+ proven ChatGPT prompts](https://magic.beehiiv.com/v1/faa6a747-8c1c-43c1-8155-91aa43268f01?email=raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com&redirect_to=https%253A%252F%252Facademy.superhuman.ai%2Fstart%3Femail%3Draiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com&utm_source=beehiiv&utm_campaign=8AWZ8QR5IO&redirect_delay=3&_bhiiv=opp_196e338b-31aa-44b3-961c-0785829b7082_d22f5b49&bhcl_id=8a0a7f24-0a83-4397-bb1b-f8d4aed155d8_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b) fix that and help you work 10X faster.\\n\\nSign up for Superhuman AI and get:\\n\\n* 1,000+ ready-to-use prompts to solve problems in minutes instead of hours\\u2014tested & used by 1M+ professionals\\n\\n* Superhuman AI newsletter (3 min daily) so you keep learning new AI tools & tutorials to stay ahead in your career\\u2014the prompts are just the beginning\\n\\n[Claim your free prompts](https://magic.beehiiv.com/v1/faa6a747-8c1c-43c1-8155-91aa43268f01?email=raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com&redirect_to=https%253A%252F%252Facademy.superhuman.ai%2Fstart%3Femail%3Draiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com&utm_source=beehiiv&utm_campaign=8AWZ8QR5IO&redirect_delay=3&_bhiiv=opp_196e338b-31aa-44b3-961c-0785829b7082_d22f5b49&bhcl_id=8a0a7f24-0a83-4397-bb1b-f8d4aed155d8_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)\\n\\n**#AD 2**\\n\\n### Take the prompts our creative team actually uses\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/9411dc7c-3dd1-4e2b-be71-0d77cfd3959b/v3-1200x600-option1__1_.png?t=1790712058)\\nFollow image link: (https://hightouch.com/amplify-your-creative-strategy-with-ai?utm_source=beehiiv&utm_medium=newsletter&utm_campaign=webinar-oct-fy27&utm_content=secondary-v2&utm_term=8AWZ8QR5IO&_bhiiv=opp_2026a625-a0d8-4936-a5e5-2cc7578a6dcf_395f767c&bhcl_id=3b123066-f5ca-48d8-bab7-3e9fcab925c8_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)\\nCaption: \\n\\nThe [key](https://hightouch.com/amplify-your-creative-strategy-with-ai?utm_source=beehiiv&utm_medium=newsletter&utm_campaign=webinar-oct-fy27&utm_content=secondary-v2&utm_term=8AWZ8QR5IO&_bhiiv=opp_2026a625-a0d8-4936-a5e5-2cc7578a6dcf_395f767c&bhcl_id=3b123066-f5ca-48d8-bab7-3e9fcab925c8_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b) to maintaining brand quality at scale? Mastering how to communicate with AI models and embedding them into your creative strategy. \\n\\nJoin our honest discussion with Ari Murray, Chief Digital Officer at Salt and Stone, and get 5 tips for expert LLM prompting with ready to run prompts. \\n\\n[Register and get the prompts](https://hightouch.com/amplify-your-creative-strategy-with-ai?utm_source=beehiiv&utm_medium=newsletter&utm_campaign=webinar-oct-fy27&utm_content=secondary-v2&utm_term=8AWZ8QR5IO&_bhiiv=opp_2026a625-a0d8-4936-a5e5-2cc7578a6dcf_395f767c&bhcl_id=3b123066-f5ca-48d8-bab7-3e9fcab925c8_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)\\n\\n\\n----------\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\nYou are reading a plain text version of this post. For the best experience, copy and paste this link in your browser to view the post online:\\nhttps://newsletter.stayingahead.com/p/claude-filed-a-murder-tip\",\n \"timeline_links\": [\n  {\n   \"communication_date\": \"2026-10-16 18:24:59\",\n   \"creation\": \"2026-10-17 16:12:08.353705\",\n   \"docstatus\": 0,\n   \"doctype\": \"Communication Link\",\n   \"idx\": 1,\n   \"link_doctype\": \"Contact\",\n   \"link_name\": \"Vaibhav\",\n   \"link_title\": \"\",\n   \"modified\": \"2026-10-17 16:12:08.353705\",\n   \"modified_by\": \"Administrator\",\n   \"name\": \"ag3hrbva9a\",\n   \"owner\": \"Administrator\",\n   \"parent\": \"ag05ge6bfv\",\n   \"parentfield\": \"timeline_links\",\n   \"parenttype\": \"Communication\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"communication_date\": \"2026-10-16 18:24:59\",\n   \"creation\": \"2026-10-17 16:12:08.354150\",\n   \"docstatus\": 0,\n   \"doctype\": \"Communication Link\",\n   \"idx\": 2,\n   \"link_doctype\": \"Contact\",\n   \"link_name\": \"Raiaayushhectocorn2029\",\n   \"link_title\": \"\",\n   \"modified\": \"2026-10-17 16:12:08.354150\",\n   \"modified_by\": \"Administrator\",\n   \"name\": \"ag3i5heui8\",\n   \"owner\": \"Administrator\",\n   \"parent\": \"ag05ge6bfv\",\n   \"parentfield\": \"timeline_links\",\n   \"parenttype\": \"Communication\"\n  }\n ],\n \"uid\": 2031,\n \"unread_notification_sent\": 0,\n \"user\": \"Administrator\"\n}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
