ine through vibrant <i>bommai golu</i> displays while the dramatic spectacle of Ramlila lights up the night sky across the Northern plains. From coast to coast, India rallies to celebrate the triumph of good over evil. And we bring you iconic sweet delicacies and <i>bhog</i> recipes\\u2014bookmark this feast issue! </p></div></section><!-- Blog-1 --><section class=\\\"blog1\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom:70px;\\\"><div style=\\\"clear:both;\\\"><div style=\\\"padding:0px 20px;\\\"><img src=\\\"https://blog.bigbasket.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/blog01_14Oct_2026.jpg\\\" style=\\\"width:100%; display:block; border-radius: 15px;\\\"></div><div style=\\\"clear: both; padding: 0px 0px 0px 140px; height: 100px; width: 549px;\\\"><div style=\\\"float:left;\\\"><span style=\\\"font-size: 70px; color:#b5d168; font-family: Arial Black,Arial Bold,Gadget,sans-serif;\\\"><b>#</b></span><span style=\\\"font-size: 115px; color:#b5d168; font-family: Arial Black,Arial Bold,Gadget,sans-serif; margin-right:15px;\\\"><b>1</b></span></div><div style=\\\"float:left; padding-top:40px; text-align:left;padding-top: 58px;\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight: bold; font-size: 22px; text-align:left;\\\">The Sweet Taste<br> of Triumph</span></div></div><div style=\\\"clear:both;\\\"></div><p style=\\\"text-align:center; margin:0px 0px 20px 0px; padding:0px 40px; font-size: 18px; line-height:32px;\\\"> Across the land, as Ravana falls and Ram ascends, and as Maa Durga claims her ultimate victory, brass platters emerge laden with the finest festive sweets. Maharashtra revels in jaggery-stuffed <i>puran poli</i>, Gujarat celebrates with <i>ghee</i>-roasted <i>mohanthal</i>, while Karnataka melts into Mysore <i>pak</i>. Today, we bring you recipes for these beloved traditional sweets from all over India.</p><a href=\\\"https://delivery.info.bigbasket.com/NQFKMIDW?id=33104=ehgCUwYAUwUCHgQPAAdSVgcHVw8HWlNTBgFSVFJUVFcLXVNQU1ZaVgBQAVUHVQlcUwFKSlULUwdIRkJaDgAFQVYHXRFbAVIHDyJSW1AMXUpSCltEBVULVAEDAgdRUFEHCVAB