a>. </p></li><li class=\\\"listItem ultext\\\"><p style=\\\"padding:0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"> TechCrunch literally called the new Decisions API <a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>OpenAI&#39;s &quot;</span></a><i><a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>Jev clone.</span></a></i><a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>&quot;</span></a> Remember Jev from last week? Yeah. </p></li><li class=\\\"listItem ultext\\\"><p style=\\\"padding:0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"> ChatGPT now suggests mid-chat plugins. <a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>One plugin&#39;s usage jumped 2,000%+</span></a>, and Greg Isenberg&#39;s already telling builders to grab the empty plugin slots before everyone else does. He&#39;s not wrong. </p></li><li class=\\\"listItem ultext\\\"><p style=\\\"padding:0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>China-linked hackers posed as a former White House AI official and a senior Anthropic employee</span></a> to phish AI policy experts. Proofpoint found it. </p></li><li class=\\\"listItem ultext\\\"><p style=\\\"padding:0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>Still no AI czar</span></a>. Trump said &quot;<i>3-4 days</i>\\u201d on Tuesday. DNI Jay Clayton is the latest name floated. </p></li></ul></div></td></tr></tbody></table></td><td width=\\\"12.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-