" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>OpenMuse</span></a></p></th></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> A Muse-style agent you host yourself. It gets a browser, your files, Gmail and Calendar, and since it&#39;s open source, your inbox never goes through Meta. </p></td></tr><tr><td style=\\\"padding-bottom:14px;padding-left:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-top:14px;\\\"><table class=\\\"table\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" style=\\\"border-bottom-width:1px;border-collapse:collapse;border-left-width:1px;border-right-width:1px;border-top-width:1px;table-layout:fixed;\\\"><tbody><tr><th class=\\\"table-h\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" valign=\\\"middle\\\" style=\\\"border-bottom-width:1px;border-left-width:1px;border-right-width:1px;border-top-width:1px;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px;\\\"><p style=\\\"padding:0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>TinyFish Monitor</span></a></p></th></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Point it at a page or topic and it only pings you when the thing you care about changes. The free launch window just ended, so it&#39;s pay per check now. </p></td></tr></tbody></table></td><td width=\\\"16\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:16px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td><td width=\\\"12.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:12.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"\\\"><tbody><tr><td height=\\\"24.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;height:24.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr><tr><td><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\"><tbody><tr><td width=\\\"12.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:12.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td><td bgcolor=\\\"transparent\\\" style=\\\"background-color:transparent;padding:0.0px 0px 0.0px 0px;box-sizing:border-box;\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"table-layout:fixed;\\\"><tbody><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;\\\"><h1 style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight:700;\\\"><b>THE SETUP</b></span></h1></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;\\\"><h3 style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight:700;\\\"><b>I made Opus 5 and 5.5 explain quantum computing</b></span></h3></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Two fresh chats, memory off, default effort, same prompts. </p></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"font-size:0px;line-height:0px;padding:12px 0px 12px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table class=\\\"j\\\" role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\"><tbody><tr><td> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;\\\"><h3 style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight:700;\\\"><b>Round 1: explain it like I&#39;m 15</b></span></h3></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight:700;\\\"><b>Prompt:</b></span> I have 20 minutes before a meeting. Explain quantum computing to me so I can explain it to a 15-year-old. I don&#39;t want a textbook explanation. Give me one analogy I can actually remember, then tell me exactly where the analogy breaks. All within 350 words max. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"></p></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-top:0px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" class=\\\"bb\\\" style=\\\"margin:0 auto 0 auto;\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" class=\\\"bb\\\" style=\\\"width:626px;\\\"><img src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80,width=1920,height=3840/uploads/asset/file/ae46c339-8b6b-44a9-9afb-e7e20e9e1351/t1.png?t=1790327750\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" height=\\\"auto\\\" width=\\\"626\\\" style=\\\"display:block;width:100%;border-radius:12px;border-style:solid;border-width:1px;box-sizing:border-box;border-color:#000000;\\\" border=\\\"0\\\"></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"></p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Both picked the same analogy: noise-cancelling headphones. Wrong answers cancel out like noise, and the right one is what&#39;s left. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Then they split. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Opus 5 talked like a friend. A normal computer walks a maze one path at a time, and a quantum computer &quot;<i>sends a wave into the maze.</i>&quot;\\u00a0 </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> It also closed with the best line in either answer: if the kid asks how the cancelling works, just say &quot;<i>I don&#39;t know, that&#39;s the hard part.</i>&quot; </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> 5.5 handed me a textbook chapter, with a big title, headings, and qubit, phase and entanglement in the first few lines.\\u00a0 </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Literally what I asked it not to do. \\ud83d\\ude43 It was more complete though, and stuck closer to my word limit (Opus 5 went about 30 over). </p></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding:12px 4px 12px 4px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\" class=\\\"d2\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#FFFFFF;border-color:#B8EF43;border-radius:0px 0px 0px 0px;border-style:solid;border-width:0px 0px 0px 2px;\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding:7px 12px 7px 12px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" class=\\\"i2\\\"><p style=\\\"color:#2D2D2D;font-weight:500;margin:0px;text-align:left;\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight:700;\\\"><b>Round 1 goes to Opus 5.</b></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"font-size:0px;line-height:0px;padding:12px 0px 12px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table class=\\\"j\\\" role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\"><tbody><tr><td> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;\\\"><h3 style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight:700;\\\"><b>Round 2: I pushed back</b></span></h3></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight:700;\\\"><b>Prompt:</b></span> That analogy makes quantum computing sound like trying lots of possibilities at once. Isn&#39;t that misleading? \\u2026 Explain what&#39;s actually different without using another analogy. All within 200 words max. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Bit unfair of me, since both had already said quantum computers don&#39;t try every answer at once. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"></p></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-top:0px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" class=\\\"bb\\\" style=\\\"margin:0 auto 0 auto;\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" class=\\\"bb\\\" style=\\\"width:626px;\\\"><img src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80,width=1920,height=3840/uploads/asset/file/cf7f667d-0254-463b-b6fc-342ef2d2240c/Frame_2147225149.png?t=1790327910\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" height=\\\"auto\\\" width=\\\"626\\\" style=\\\"display:block;width:100%;border-radius:12px;border-style:solid;border-width:1px;box-sizing:border-box;border-color:#000000;\\\" border=\\\"0\\\"></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"></p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Opus 5 took the blame anyway (&quot;the fault was mine&quot;), then lost me with &quot;one reversible linear operation to the entire amplitude vector.&quot; Try saying that to a 15-year-old. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> 5.5 agreed with the fair part, reminded me it had already covered this, and kept it plain: a normal computer&#39;s odds can only add up, while a quantum computer&#39;s numbers can go negative and cancel out. </p></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding:12px 4px 12px 4px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\" class=\\\"d2\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#FFFFFF;border-color:#B8EF43;border-radius:0px 0px 0px 0px;border-style:solid;border-width:0px 0px 0px 2px;\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding:7px 12px 7px 12px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" class=\\\"i2\\\"><p style=\\\"color:#2D2D2D;font-weight:500;margin:0px;text-align:left;\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight:700;\\\"><b>Round 2 goes to 5.5, easily.</b></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"><b>The bill:</b> Opus 5 cost $0.072 and 5.5 cost $0.055, about a quarter cheaper. Token counts were nearly identical, so that&#39;s mostly the price cut. </p></td></tr></tbody></table></td><td width=\\\"12.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:12.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td height=\\\"24.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;height:24.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"\\\"><tbody><tr><td><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\"><tbody><tr><td width=\\\"12.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:12.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td><td bgcolor=\\\"transparent\\\" style=\\\"background-color:transparent;border-color:#000000;border-radius:8px;border-style:solid;border-width:2px;padding:16.0px 0px 16.0px 0px;box-sizing:border-box;\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"table-layout:fixed;\\\"><tbody><tr><td width=\\\"16\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:16px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td><td><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"table-layout:fixed;\\\"><tbody><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;\\\"><h1 style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;\\\"><b>My Take</b></h1></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> I went in expecting 5.5 to sweep but it didn&#39;t. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Opus 5, the model everyone called annoying, still writes the warmer first draft and the line I&#39;d use. But push it once and it apologises and starts lecturing, while 5.5 gets calmer and clearer. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> So maybe the upgrade is a better second answer. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> In July I said the fight had moved to price, speed and tone. 5.5 wins on price, but on tone, I\\u2019m split. And one run each proves very little. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Remember the DNA find? Spotted once, missed ten times in a row. </p></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding:12px 4px 12px 4px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\" class=\\\"d2\\\" style=\\\"background-color:#FFFFFF;border-color:#B8EF43;border-radius:0px 0px 0px 0px;border-style:solid;border-width:0px 0px 0px 2px;\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding:7px 12px 7px 12px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" class=\\\"i2\\\"><p style=\\\"color:#2D2D2D;font-weight:500;margin:0px;text-align:left;\\\"><span style=\\\"font-weight:700;\\\"><b>5.5 is my default for now.</b></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Your homework: ask both the same question, push back once, and see which one you&#39;d trust with your second message. Then reply and tell me which explanation you&#39;d have used. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"><b>Until next time, </b><br><b>Vaibhav \\ud83e\\udd1d\\ud83c\\udffb</b></p></td></tr></tbody></table></td><td width=\\\"16\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:16px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td><td width=\\\"12.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:12.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"\\\"><tbody><tr><td height=\\\"24.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;height:24.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr><tr><td><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\"><tbody><tr><td width=\\\"12.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:12.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td><td bgcolor=\\\"transparent\\\" style=\\\"background-color:transparent;border-bottom-left-radius:12px;border-bottom-right-radius:12px;border-bottom-width:2px;border-color:#6FE394;border-left-width:2px;border-right-width:2px;border-style:dashed;border-top-left-radius:12px;border-top-right-radius:12px;border-top-width:2px;padding:16.0px 0px 16.0px 0px;box-sizing:border-box;\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"table-layout:fixed;\\\"><tbody><tr><td width=\\\"16\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:16px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td><td><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"table-layout:fixed;\\\"><tbody><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"><b>If you read till here, you might find this interesting</b><br><br><b>#AD 1</b></p></td></tr><tr><td id=\\\"the-agentic-era-needs-a-different-c\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;\\\"><h3 style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;\\\">The agentic era needs a different CRM. That\\u2019s Attio.</h3></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-top:0px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" class=\\\"bb\\\" style=\\\"margin:0 auto 0 auto;\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" class=\\\"bb\\\" style=\\\"width:594px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\" style=\\\"text-decoration:none;\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\"><img src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80,width=1920,height=3840/uploads/asset/file/411ee7dc-ae18-4da1-830b-c784f0164c10/Copy_of_1920x1080-1.png?t=1789142762\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" height=\\\"auto\\\" width=\\\"594\\\" style=\\\"display:block;width:100%;\\\" border=\\\"0\\\"></a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Teams like Parallel, Turbopuffer, and Wordsmith are already setting the pace on <a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>Attio</span></a>. Get an always-on revenue engine, with agents and workflows that build pipeline, chase every buying signal, and move deals forward with your team. Whether you&#39;re working in your browser, inbox, or favorite agent, connect to your customer data in real-time through Attio&#39;s web app, MCP, API, and SDK. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"><a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>Try Attio now</span></a></p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"><b>#AD 2</b></p></td></tr><tr><td id=\\\"most-founders-are-one-system-away-f\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;\\\"><h3 style=\\\"color:#000000;font-weight:400;\\\">Most founders are one system away from turning LinkedIn into their best sales channel.</h3></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-top:0px;\\\" class=\\\"dd\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" class=\\\"bb\\\" style=\\\"margin:0 auto 0 auto;\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" class=\\\"bb\\\" style=\\\"width:594px;\\\"><img src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80,width=1920,height=3840/uploads/asset/file/792f1079-cc67-42e1-8acc-bef99ed77e84/Copy_of_Beehive_AEO_for_Lean_Teams__1200___628___1_.png?t=1789776819\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" height=\\\"auto\\\" width=\\\"594\\\" style=\\\"display:block;width:100%;\\\" border=\\\"0\\\"></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Engagement is easy to mistake for pipeline. On Sep 30, <a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>watch how</span></a> a founder turns LinkedIn content into real outreach. Live. You&#39;ll walk away with a repeatable system: what to post, who to reach out to, and how to sequence it.\\u00a0 </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"> Eligible startups also get the LinkedIn-to-Leads Toolkit: ad credits, Apollo, Captions, and HubSpot&#39;s Prospecting Agent. </p></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"dd\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;\\\"><p style=\\\"\\\"><i><a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\\\"><span>Claim my spot</span></a></i></p></td></tr></tbody></table></td><td width=\\\"16\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:16px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td><td width=\\\"12.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;width:12.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td height=\\\"24.0px\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;height:24.0px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\"><tbody><tr><td></td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"b\\\" align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#030712\\\" style=\\\"padding:0px 0px 0px 0px;border-style:solid;border-width: 0px 0px 0px 0px;border-color: #FFFFFF;border-bottom-left-radius:10px;border-bottom-right-radius:10px;\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#B8EF43\\\" style=\\\"padding:12px;\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\"><tbody><tr><td><span style=\\\"padding-left:1px;\\\"></span></td><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"middle\\\" width=\\\"75\\\" style=\\\"width:75px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" style=\\\"text-decoration:none;\\\"><img width=\\\"22\\\" height=\\\"22\\\" alt=\\\"tw\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"display:block;max-width:22px;color:Dark;\\\" src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/static_assets/x_dark.png\\\"></a></td><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"middle\\\" width=\\\"75\\\" style=\\\"width:75px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" style=\\\"text-decoration:none;\\\"><img width=\\\"22\\\" height=\\\"22\\\" alt=\\\"ig\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"display:block;max-width:22px;color:Dark;\\\" src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/static_assets/instagram_dark.png\\\"></a></td><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"middle\\\" width=\\\"75\\\" style=\\\"width:75px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" style=\\\"text-decoration:none;\\\"><img width=\\\"22\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" alt=\\\"yt\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"display:block;max-width:22px;color:Dark;\\\" src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/static_assets/youtube_dark.png\\\"></a></td><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"middle\\\" width=\\\"75\\\" style=\\\"width:75px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" style=\\\"text-decoration:none;\\\"><img width=\\\"22\\\" height=\\\"22\\\" alt=\\\"in\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"display:block;max-width:22px;color:Dark;\\\" src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/static_assets/linkedin_dark.png\\\"></a></td><td><span style=\\\"padding-left:1px;\\\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td height=\\\"10\\\" style=\\\"line-height:1px;font-size:1px;height:10px;\\\"> &nbsp; </td></tr><tr><td class=\\\"w\\\" align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding:15px 15px 15px 15px;\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\"><tbody><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"><p style=\'font-family:\\\"Verdana\\\",Geneva,sans-serif;color:#FFFFFF!important;\'> Update your email preferences or unsubscribe <a class=\\\"link\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\" style=\\\"text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:#FFFFFF!important;color:#FFFFFF!important;\\\"> here</a></p><p class=\\\"copyright\\\" style=\'font-family:\\\"Verdana\\\",Geneva,sans-serif;color:#FFFFFF!important;\'> &copy; 2026 Staying Ahead with AI </p><p style=\'font-family:\\\"Verdana\\\",Geneva,sans-serif;color:#FFFFFF!important;\'> 228 Park Ave S, #29976, New York, New York 10003, United States </p></td></tr><tr style=\\\"display: table-row !important;\\\"><td align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" style=\\\"padding-top:20px;\\\"><table role=\\\"none\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"0\\\" align=\\\"center\\\" style=\\\"display:table !important;\\\"><tbody><tr style=\\\"display:table-row !important;\\\"><td class=\\\"u\\\" align=\\\"center\\\" valign=\\\"middle\\\" height=\\\"32\\\" style=\\\"height:32px;display:table-cell !important; max-height: 32px !important;margin:0px !important; background-color: #ffffff !important;\\\"><a style=\\\"line-height:32px !important;text-decoration:none;display:block !important;\\\" href=\\\"https://link.mail.beehiiv.\\\"><img width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" alt=\\\"beehiiv logo\\\" style=\\\"display:inline-block !important;max-width:16px !important;vertical-align:-3px !important;width:16px !important;height:16px !important;\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" src=\\\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=pad,format=png,onerror=redirect,quality=100,width=16,height=16,gravity=center,background=transparent,dpr=2/output-onlinepngtools.png\\\"><span style=\\\"padding-left:11px !important;display: inline-block !important;\\\">Powered by beehiiv</span></a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" height=\\\"2\\\" style=\\\"height:2px;line-height:1px;font-size:1px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://hp.beehiiv.com/1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4\\\" style=\\\"color: #030712 !important; cursor: default; font-size: 1px; text-decoration: none;\\\"></a></td></tr><tr><td align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\" height=\\\"2\\\" style=\\\"height:2px;\\\"><a href=\\\"https://email.beehiivstatus.com/8c7a217d64c9829875741fc43c7b9b540b5ee87b/hclick\\\" style=\\\"color: #030712 !important; cursor: default; font-size: 1px; text-decoration: none;\\\"></a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\",\n \"creation\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:51.042366\",\n \"delivery_status\": \"\",\n \"docstatus\": 0,\n \"doctype\": \"Communication\",\n \"email_account\": \"sales\",\n \"email_status\": \"Open\",\n \"email_template\": null,\n \"feedback_request\": null,\n \"has_attachment\": 0,\n \"idx\": 0,\n \"imap_folder\": null,\n \"in_reply_to\": null,\n \"message_id\": \"20260925.125848.c7a4be8a@mta15\",\n \"modified\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:51.202036\",\n \"modified_by\": \"Administrator\",\n \"name\": \"aamo78nh2c\",\n \"owner\": \"Administrator\",\n \"phone_no\": null,\n \"rating\": 0,\n \"read_by_recipient\": 0,\n \"read_by_recipient_on\": null,\n \"read_receipt\": 0,\n \"recipients\": \"\\\"raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com\\\" <raiaayushhectocorn2029@gmail.com>\",\n \"reference_doctype\": \"CRM Lead\",\n \"reference_name\": \"CRM-LEAD-2026-00052\",\n \"reference_owner\": \"Administrator\",\n \"seen\": 0,\n \"send_after\": null,\n \"sender\": \"vaibhav@outskillwithai.com\",\n \"sender_full_name\": \"Vaibhav Sisinty\",\n \"sent_or_received\": \"Received\",\n \"status\": \"Linked\",\n \"subject\": \"anthropic lied?\",\n \"text_content\": \"----------\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/06e9e26b-31e3-41b9-8d33-1e4fc1dccda7/Frame_2147225035.png?t=1785742897)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n\\n--------------------\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\nI\'m unable to make up my mind on what to write today.\\n\\nAnthropic shipped Opus 5.5 on Tuesday and OpenAI replied the same day with two cheaper GPT-6 models.\\n\\nA day later, the heads of both labs were at the UN asking for guardrails. Meanwhile Claude found something weird in viral DNA, and Meta put its AI agent on a keychain.\\n\\nPick one? I couldn\'t.\\n\\nSo I went back to July. When Opus 5 launched, [reviewers called it neurotic](https://www.chatprd.ai/how-i-ai/my-surprising-verdict-on-claude-opus-5), so I [tested it myself](https://newsletter.stayingahead.com/p/opus-vs-me). Now Anthropic says 5.5 [explains things more clearly](https://www.anthropic.com/claude-opus-5-5), puts the important stuff first and cuts the jargon.\\n\\nBig claim. So I put both in the ring. **But first, the catch-up.**\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **NEWS CATCH-UP**\\n\\n**GPT-6 got cheaper.** Sol and Luna cost half of what they replace. Catch: for now they [only live in Codex and ChatGPT Work](https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/22/openai-upgrading-chatgpt-and-codex-with-two-more-gpt-6-models/), so you\'ll have to go looking.\\n\\n**ChatGPT Voice can use your apps.** It now [pulls from your email, calendar and Slack](https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/23/openai-just-upgraded-chatgpt-voice-in-three-ways/), so \\\"what does tomorrow look like?\\\" finally gets an answer.\\n\\n**The AI bosses went to the UN.** Altman and Amodei briefed the Security Council on Wednesday. Altman\'s headline: \\\"[We could lose control of the future to AI.](https://openai.com/index/sam-altman-un-security-council-remarks/)\\\" This was a day after both made their AI cheaper for everyone. Great timing. \\ud83d\\ude05\\n\\n**Meta went all in on Muse.** It can now [use apps on your Mac](https://www.meta.com/blog/meta-connect-2026-everything-we-announced/) and shop for you, and it\'s getting its own email address. Can\'t wait? [Instinct](https://www.mager.co/blog/2026-09-12-instinct/) already does this over iMessage and WhatsApp (invite-only though).\\n\\n\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/734d3ae8-cb5d-4096-b3cf-675205e60e7a/Frame_2147225127.png?t=1790322629)\\nFollow image link: (https://www.meta.com/blog/meta-vr-glasses-announcement-meta-connect/)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n\\n**Claude found an enzyme system nobody had seen before.** [Claude agents](https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-discovers-novel-enzyme-system) were digging through viral DNA and spotted CRISPR-like repeats in the raw data. Nobody knows what it does yet, and 10 reruns of the same search missed it completely. (hold onto that one)\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **QUICK HITS**\\n\\n* Claude Code cloud sessions are out of preview, with free credit ($100 on Pro, $250 on Max) if you claim by Oct 7 \\u2192 [Claim here](https://x.com/ClaudeDevs/status/2102871550974427462)\\n\\n* Opus 5.5 hands most cybersecurity requests to the older Opus 4.8 \\u2192 [Read](https://the-decoder.com/claude-opus-5-5-matches-fable-5-1-at-40-percent-lower-cost-as-anthropic-promises-to-fix-claudish-writing/)\\n\\n* Keep Opus 5.5 off max effort. Simon Willison asked it for one pelican drawing and it thought for nearly 20 minutes, costing $2.56. Most expensive bird ever \\u2192 [Read](https://simonwillison.net/2026/Sep/22/opus-and-sol-and-luna/)\\n\\n* Adobe put Acrobat inside Claude, so you can edit PDFs without leaving the chat \\u2192 [Read](https://blog.adobe.com/en/publish/2026/09/24/adobe-comes-to-gemini-expands-what-you-can-do-in-claude)\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **TOOLS ON MY RADAR**\\n\\n[Gemini 3.8 Flash TTS](https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/gemini-3-8-text-to-speech/)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nDescribe a voice in plain words and it builds it. 2,000+ voices, 100+ languages, and it can clone yours from a 30-second clip. Already in Gemini Notebook.\\n\\n[OpenMuse](https://www.scriptbyai.com/openmuse-personal-ai-agents/)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nA Muse-style agent you host yourself. It gets a browser, your files, Gmail and Calendar, and since it\'s open source, your inbox never goes through Meta.\\n\\n[TinyFish Monitor](https://www.tinyfish.ai/blog/introducing-tinyfish-monitor-subscribe-to-the-web)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nPoint it at a page or topic and it only pings you when the thing you care about changes. The free launch window just ended, so it\'s pay per check now.\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **THE SETUP**\\n\\n### **I made Opus 5 and 5.5 explain quantum computing**\\n\\nTwo fresh chats, memory off, default effort, same prompts.\\n\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n### **Round 1: explain it like I\'m 15**\\n\\n**Prompt:** I have 20 minutes before a meeting. Explain quantum computing to me so I can explain it to a 15-year-old. I don\'t want a textbook explanation. Give me one analogy I can actually remember, then tell me exactly where the analogy breaks. All within 350 words max.\\n\\n\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/ae46c339-8b6b-44a9-9afb-e7e20e9e1351/t1.png?t=1790327750)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n\\nBoth picked the same analogy: noise-cancelling headphones. Wrong answers cancel out like noise, and the right one is what\'s left.\\n\\nThen they split.\\n\\nOpus 5 talked like a friend. A normal computer walks a maze one path at a time, and a quantum computer \\\"_sends a wave into the maze._\\\"\\u00a0\\n\\nIt also closed with the best line in either answer: if the kid asks how the cancelling works, just say \\\"_I don\'t know, that\'s the hard part._\\\"\\n\\n5.5 handed me a textbook chapter, with a big title, headings, and qubit, phase and entanglement in the first few lines.\\u00a0\\n\\nLiterally what I asked it not to do. \\ud83d\\ude43 It was more complete though, and stuck closer to my word limit (Opus 5 went about 30 over).\\n\\n\\u201c**Round 1 goes to Opus 5.**\\u201c \\u2014 \\n\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\n### **Round 2: I pushed back**\\n\\n**Prompt:** That analogy makes quantum computing sound like trying lots of possibilities at once. Isn\'t that misleading? \\u2026 Explain what\'s actually different without using another analogy. All within 200 words max.\\n\\nBit unfair of me, since both had already said quantum computers don\'t try every answer at once.\\n\\n\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/cf7f667d-0254-463b-b6fc-342ef2d2240c/Frame_2147225149.png?t=1790327910)\\nCaption: \\n\\n\\n\\nOpus 5 took the blame anyway (\\\"the fault was mine\\\"), then lost me with \\\"one reversible linear operation to the entire amplitude vector.\\\" Try saying that to a 15-year-old.\\n\\n5.5 agreed with the fair part, reminded me it had already covered this, and kept it plain: a normal computer\'s odds can only add up, while a quantum computer\'s numbers can go negative and cancel out.\\n\\n\\u201c**Round 2 goes to 5.5, easily.**\\u201c \\u2014 \\n\\n**The bill:** Opus 5 cost $0.072 and 5.5 cost $0.055, about a quarter cheaper. Token counts were nearly identical, so that\'s mostly the price cut.\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n# **My Take**\\n\\nI went in expecting 5.5 to sweep but it didn\'t.\\n\\nOpus 5, the model everyone called annoying, still writes the warmer first draft and the line I\'d use. But push it once and it apologises and starts lecturing, while 5.5 gets calmer and clearer.\\n\\nSo maybe the upgrade is a better second answer.\\n\\nIn July I said the fight had moved to price, speed and tone. 5.5 wins on price, but on tone, I\\u2019m split. And one run each proves very little.\\n\\nRemember the DNA find? Spotted once, missed ten times in a row.\\n\\n\\u201c**5.5 is my default for now.**\\u201c \\u2014 \\n\\nYour homework: ask both the same question, push back once, and see which one you\'d trust with your second message. Then reply and tell me which explanation you\'d have used.\\n\\n**Until next time, **\\n**Vaibhav \\ud83e\\udd1d\\ud83c\\udffb**\\n\\n\\n--------------------\\n**If you read till here, you might find this interesting**\\n\\n**#AD 1**\\n\\n### The agentic era needs a different CRM. That\\u2019s Attio.\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/411ee7dc-ae18-4da1-830b-c784f0164c10/Copy_of_1920x1080-1.png?t=1789142762)\\nFollow image link: (https://attio.com/?utm_source=beehiiv&utm_medium=newsletter_sponsorship&utm_campaign=beehiiv-Y26&utm_content=8AWZ8QR5IO&_bhiiv=opp_e3b8d67a-a21d-4f1e-a564-6fc2a364512f_7395cee5&bhcl_id=7ce61d76-99e4-41f9-88a3-e824364a5625_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)\\nCaption: \\n\\nTeams like Parallel, Turbopuffer, and Wordsmith are already setting the pace on [Attio](https://attio.com/?utm_source=beehiiv&utm_medium=newsletter_sponsorship&utm_campaign=beehiiv-Y26&utm_content=8AWZ8QR5IO&_bhiiv=opp_e3b8d67a-a21d-4f1e-a564-6fc2a364512f_7395cee5&bhcl_id=7ce61d76-99e4-41f9-88a3-e824364a5625_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b). Get an always-on revenue engine, with agents and workflows that build pipeline, chase every buying signal, and move deals forward with your team. Whether you\'re working in your browser, inbox, or favorite agent, connect to your customer data in real-time through Attio\'s web app, MCP, API, and SDK.\\n\\n[Try Attio now](https://attio.com/?utm_source=beehiiv&utm_medium=newsletter_sponsorship&utm_campaign=beehiiv-Y26&utm_content=8AWZ8QR5IO&_bhiiv=opp_e3b8d67a-a21d-4f1e-a564-6fc2a364512f_7395cee5&bhcl_id=7ce61d76-99e4-41f9-88a3-e824364a5625_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)\\n\\n**#AD 2**\\n\\n### Most founders are one system away from turning LinkedIn into their best sales channel.\\n\\nView image: (https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/792f1079-cc67-42e1-8acc-bef99ed77e84/Copy_of_Beehive_AEO_for_Lean_Teams__1200___628___1_.png?t=1789776819)\\nCaption: \\n\\nEngagement is easy to mistake for pipeline. On Sep 30, [watch how](https://offers.hubspot.com/startups/linkedin-lead-engine?utm_medium=email-media-newsletter&utm_source=mindstream&utm_campaign=owned&utm_content=september_webinar&utm_term=8AWZ8QR5IO_HSFSSecondaryLinkedInWebinarV2&_bhiiv=opp_ca801f65-f9e1-488d-8f2f-91c0d3920cd6_da2740b6&bhcl_id=11ece94e-f3e1-47ae-89c4-149521347856_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b) a founder turns LinkedIn content into real outreach. Live. You\'ll walk away with a repeatable system: what to post, who to reach out to, and how to sequence it.\\u00a0\\n\\nEligible startups also get the LinkedIn-to-Leads Toolkit: ad credits, Apollo, Captions, and HubSpot\'s Prospecting Agent.\\n\\n_[Claim my spot](https://offers.hubspot.com/startups/linkedin-lead-engine?utm_medium=email-media-newsletter&utm_source=mindstream&utm_campaign=owned&utm_content=september_webinar&utm_term=8AWZ8QR5IO_HSFSSecondaryLinkedInWebinarV2&_bhiiv=opp_ca801f65-f9e1-488d-8f2f-91c0d3920cd6_da2740b6&bhcl_id=11ece94e-f3e1-47ae-89c4-149521347856_1ecd4f85-bc08-4bd0-a10f-628117366dd4_ef7bc386-7a60-4bb7-a72a-41016dc7825b)_\\n\\n\\n----------\\n\\u2014\\u2014\\u2014\\n\\nYou are reading a plain text version of this post. For the best experience, copy and paste this link in your browser to view the post online:\\nhttps://newsletter.stayingahead.com/p/anthropic-lied\",\n \"timeline_links\": [\n  {\n   \"communication_date\": \"2026-09-25 18:28:48\",\n   \"creation\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:51.310074\",\n   \"docstatus\": 0,\n   \"doctype\": \"Communication Link\",\n   \"idx\": 1,\n   \"link_doctype\": \"Contact\",\n   \"link_name\": \"Vaibhav\",\n   \"link_title\": \"\",\n   \"modified\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:51.310074\",\n   \"modified_by\": \"Administrator\",\n   \"name\": \"aapngcjbu7\",\n   \"owner\": \"Administrator\",\n   \"parent\": \"aamo78nh2c\",\n   \"parentfield\": \"timeline_links\",\n   \"parenttype\": \"Communication\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"communication_date\": \"2026-09-25 18:28:48\",\n   \"creation\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:51.310521\",\n   \"docstatus\": 0,\n   \"doctype\": \"Communication Link\",\n   \"idx\": 2,\n   \"link_doctype\": \"Contact\",\n   \"link_name\": \"Raiaayushhectocorn2029\",\n   \"link_title\": \"\",\n   \"modified\": \"2026-10-17 16:11:51.310521\",\n   \"modified_by\": \"Administrator\",\n   \"name\": \"aapkjoamf2\",\n   \"owner\": \"Administrator\",\n   \"parent\": \"aamo78nh2c\",\n   \"parentfield\": \"timeline_links\",\n   \"parenttype\": \"Communication\"\n  }\n ],\n \"uid\": 1957,\n \"unread_notification_sent\": 0,\n \"user\": \"Administrator\"\n}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
